Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:13:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 231/231] Meridian: a settings glow-up event with no BrowserView to
 hear it is skipped, not fatal

Picking another search engine in chrome://settings/search called
SetDefaultSearchEngine, whose MaybeNotifySettingsCustomEvent CHECK'd
that kBrowserViewElementId resolves to an element. That element is
tracked by views::BrowserView alone, and Meridian's window is the WebUI,
so the CHECK took the browser down (SIGABRT). The sibling
MaybeNotifySettingsElementActivated already skips a missing element, so
the custom-event path now does the same; ClearBrowsingDataHandler's
identical NotifyBrowserViewCustomEvent too.
---
 .../webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc  | 6 +++++-
 chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_utils.cc          | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc
index c30225a50c..d6b4e41537 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,11 @@ void NotifyBrowserViewCustomEvent(tabs::TabInterface* tab,
   ui::TrackedElement* const browser_element =
       ui::ElementTracker::GetElementTracker()->GetUniqueElement(
           kBrowserViewElementId, context);
-  CHECK(browser_element);
+  // The browser element is tracked only where a views::BrowserView exists. A
+  // window built any other way has nothing to notify, so the event is skipped.
+  if (!browser_element) {
+    return;
+  }
   ui::ElementTracker::GetFrameworkDelegate()->NotifyCustomEvent(browser_element,
                                                                 event_type);
 }
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_utils.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_utils.cc
index 352e5946c8..a8acc50294 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_utils.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_utils.cc
@@ -50,7 +50,11 @@ void MaybeNotifySettingsCustomEvent(content::WebUI* web_ui,
   ui::TrackedElement* const browser_element =
       ui::ElementTracker::GetElementTracker()->GetUniqueElement(
           kBrowserViewElementId, context);
-  CHECK(browser_element);
+  // The browser element is tracked only where a views::BrowserView exists. A
+  // window built any other way has nothing to notify, so the event is skipped.
+  if (!browser_element) {
+    return;
+  }
   ui::ElementTracker::GetFrameworkDelegate()->NotifyCustomEvent(browser_element,
                                                                 event_type);
 }
